          "note": "Comparative Ryukyuan evidence and Ainu loans point to an earlier stop *p; word-initial p had become [ɸ] by Early Middle Japanese, rendered as f in 16th-century Portuguese works. Before u the [ɸ] survives in Modern Japanese; scholars disagree on whether the lenition had already happened within the Old Japanese period."
